menu "ESP Thread Border Router Web"

    config ESP_BR_WEB_CLI
        bool "Enable Web CLI and BR log capture"
        depends on OPENTHREAD_BR_START_WEB
        default n
        help
            Show a Web CLI in Tools and capture recent BR logs in RAM.
            OpenThread command execution additionally requires OPENTHREAD_CLI.
            Disabling this option excludes the backend, log buffer and CLI
            callback wrappers. The serial console is unaffected.

    config ESP_BR_WEB_CLI_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "Web CLI log buffer size in bytes"
        depends on ESP_BR_WEB_CLI
        range 1024 65536
        default 16384
        help
            Fixed RAM byte ring holding variable-length output fragments.
            Each fragment uses 12 bytes of metadata plus its actual text length
            (up to 255 bytes), without padding or a terminating NUL. Oldest
            whole fragments are overwritten when space is needed. Reading
            does not remove data, so clients have independent cursors.
            Defaults to 16 KiB. Ring bookkeeping and HTTP JSON responses use
            additional memory. Replaces ESP_BR_WEB_CLI_RECORD_COUNT; existing
            configurations should select a byte budget instead of a count.

endmenu
